    {
     "id": "/page/0/Text/17",
     "block_type": "Text",
     "html": "<p>The prior example admitted no issues of compatibility between different rays of the same cone. This is not ordinarily the case; if <math>\\rho_1 = \\mathbb{R}_+(a_1x_1 + \\dots + a_nx_n)</math> and <math>\\rho_2 = \\mathbb{R}_+(b_1x_1 + \\dots + b_nx_n)</math>, compatibility is less common if the linear matroid on the <math>n</math> vectors</p>",
     "polygon": [
